 c in json.load(sys.stdin)['commits'][:1]: print(c['author']['date'], c['message'][:500])\" forge -R world/idea-repo api 'repos/worl…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "forge -R world/idea-repo api 'repos/world/idea-repo/wiki/revisions/Brief' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nfor c in json.load(sys.stdin)['commits'][:1]: print(c['author']['date'], c['message'][:500])\"\nforge -R world/idea-repo api 'repos/world/idea-repo/wiki/page/Brief' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json,base64\nt=base64.b64decode(json.load(sys.stdin)['content_base64']).decode();open('/hutian/w/brief8.md','w').write(t)\"\ndiff /hutian/w/brief7.md /hutian/w/brief8.md | cut -c1-2500\nforge -R world/story-repo api 'repos/world/story-repo/wiki/revisions/Outline' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nfor c in json.load(sys.stdin)['commits'][:1]: print(c['author']['date'], c['message'][:500])\"\nforge -R world/story-repo api 'repos/world/story-repo/issues/9/comments' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nfor c in json.load(sys.stdin): print(c['user']['login'],c['body'][:2000])\""], ["timeout", "90000"]], "output": "```console\n2026-11-26T08:28:00Z Brief rev 8: H2 via SE ratio and matched contrasts, Delta as low-power gauge; (5) wording per review\n\n17c17\n< - H2 (design vs statistics): differences between designs in Q (and in k\\*/(z√N)) beyond z and density are due to *misfit*, measured with the parametric-bootstrap null below; if Real − Null ≈ 0 for a design, its fragility is purely statistical.\n---\n> - H2 (design vs statistics), restated in rev 8 after the positive control (`experiment-repo`#9): a design can matter for fragility through (a) the *margin* z (its SE, i.e. the clustering design effect = cluster-bootstrap SE / model SE) or (b) *misfit* that moves k\\* at fixed z. (a) is measured by the **SE ratio** and by the matched contrasts (same battles/pairs, different judges, joint resampling). (b) is gauged by Δ(log Q) = Real − Null on the same graph, **but the positive control shows Δ does not respond to any injected departure tried** (overdispersion, position bias, cycle, pair-specific deviation; |Δ| ≤ 0.04 while the SE ratio moves 0.82 → 2.26), so Δ ≈ 0 says only that real k\\* follows the same-graph null as the null follows itself (a statement about the margin), not that BT fits. H2 is therefore tested through the SE ratio and the matched contrasts, with Δ reported as a gauge of limited power.\n51c51\n< To our knowledge, among the sources we could consult: (1) a common scale for noise and intent (SE-unit fragility F, its ratio to the null, P_flip curves); (2) design-vs-statistics separation by matched contrasts and a parametric-bootstrap null; (3) search-vs-exact sandwich for fragility; (4) CI-separated ≠ robust, quantified per design as a curve; (5) a calibration, out of sample, of what predicts k*: held-out comparison of the regression rule, the same-graph null's k*, the rescaled first-order influence estimate, log z alone and the intercept (log z carries most of it; N, density and ties add little beyond the same-graph reference; k* is predicted to a factor of about 1.3 from one influence computation, without search). \"Dropping a few votes changes the top model\" is a replication-type observation inside (1), not the headline.\n---\n> To our knowledge, among the sources we could consult: (1) a common scale for noise and intent (SE-unit fragility F, its ratio to the null, P_flip curves); (2) design-vs-statistics separation by matched contrasts, the SE ratio (design effect) and a parametric-bootstrap null, with the positive control showing which of these instruments can see a departure (the SE ratio can, Δ(log Q) cannot); (3) search-vs-exact sandwich for fragility; (4) CI-separated ≠ robust, quantified per design as a curve; (5) a calibration, out of sample, of what predicts k*: held-out comparison of the regression rule, the same-graph null's k*, the rescaled first-order influence estimate, log z alone and the intercept (log z carries most of it; N, density and ties add little beyond the same-graph reference; flips are predicted to a factor of about 1.2 from one influence computation plus a median-bias rescale, whose constant is fitted on the other data sets; deletion to about 1.3 from the fitted rule or the null reference, which needs a search on null replicates; the rescaled first-order estimate is worse for deletion, RMSE 0.38). \"Dropping a few votes changes the top model\" is a replication-type observation inside (1), not the headline.\n56,57c56,57\n< - F/z matches the null and Real − Null ≈ 0: main finding \"fragility is statistical: set by z and N, not by who judges\", with the collapse and predictive rule as the deliverable.\n< - Real − Null > 0 in some designs: the finding is which misfit (position/length bias, draws, schedule) carries it, shown on the matched contrasts.\n---\n> - F/z matches the null and Real − Null ≈ 0 (rev 8: this alone does not show BT fits, since Δ has no power against the departures tried; the SE ratio and matched contrasts carry the design claim): main finding \"fragility is statistical: set by z and N, not by who ju\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "b00d2c8a-993d-5a3b-a00c-019f0fb12241", "at": 1795681910.604286, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 77223, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "4c0f0de9776b93ba51bdbd6026abd40b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "9c85b312-64c5-5f7d-bcaa-3dc5fbe88bc2", "at": 1795681910.6525476, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 77224, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "4c0f0de9776b93ba51bdbd6026abd40b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": nul